      "obligation": "refuter:12:1",
      "id": "lem-dj-bridge-integral-murphy-and-polytabloid-straightening",
      "location": "Proof 1.3",
      "defect": "unlicensed-inference",
      "evidence": "The proof says that w_lambda^{-1} is increasing on each mu-block. For lambda=(3,2), mu=(2,2,1), the row-filled tableau has rows [1,2,3]/[4,5], the column-filled tableau has rows [1,3,5]/[2,4], and the stipulated w_lambda is (1,4,2,5,3). Thus w_lambda^{-1} takes 3,4 in the block {3,4} to 5,2, which is not increasing. This does not license the ensuing length-additivity application to u^{-1}w_lambda^{-1}; the needed true property is that w_lambda is increasing on the mu-blocks. The direction error is readily corrected.",
      "severity": "nonfatal",
      "observed_sha256": "28141c4251f131085ff552c476662148c8b4c85898a7283e8f953a9938183caa"
    },
    {
      "obligation": "refuter:12:2",
      "id": "lem-dj-bridge-integral-murphy-and-polytabloid-straightening",
      "location": "Proof 2.2",
      "defect": "unlicensed-inference",
      "evidence": "The cited dependency lem-dj-bridge-sign-automorphism-and-star-dual states its identity for “every partition lambda⊢n,” while alpha here is a Garnir composition. The proof uses theta(x_alpha)=q^{N_alpha}y_alpha without defining or deriving the composition case. Extending the same eigenspace argument to the parabolic subgroup S_alpha would close this short gap, but the cited statement alone does not justify the step.",
